{"instance_id": "HardcodedDebugModeDetector:HardcodedDebugMode", "issue_id": "HardcodedDebugMode", "detector": "HardcodedDebugModeDetector", "check_file": "HardcodedDebugModeDetector.java", "check_lang": "java", "test_file": "HardcodedDebugModeDetectorTest.kt", "check_url": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/tools/base/+/refs/heads/mirror-goog-studio-main/lint/libs/lint-checks/src/main/java/com/android/tools/lint/checks/HardcodedDebugModeDetector.java", "test_url": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/tools/base/+/refs/heads/mirror-goog-studio-main/lint/libs/lint-tests/src/test/java/com/android/tools/lint/checks/HardcodedDebugModeDetectorTest.kt", "methods_to_generate": ["getApplicableAttributes", "visitAttribute"], "tests_to_run": ["testOk", "testNoNS"], "brief_description": "Hardcoded value of `android:debuggable` in the manifest", "explanation": "It's best to leave out the `android:debuggable` attribute from the manifest.  If you do, then the tools will automatically insert `android:debuggable=true` when  building an APK to debug on an emulator or device. And when you perform a  release build, such as Exporting APK, it will automatically set it to `false`.n n If on the other hand you specify a specific value in the manifest file, then  the tools will always use it. This can lead to accidentally publishing  your app with debug information.", "nl_spec": "Hardcoded value of `android:debuggable` in the manifest\n\nIt's best to leave out the `android:debuggable` attribute from the manifest.  If you do, then the tools will automatically insert `android:debuggable=true` when  building an APK to debug on an emulator or device. And when you perform a  release build, such as Exporting APK, it will automatically set it to `false`.n n If on the other hand you specify a specific value in the manifest file, then  the tools will always use it. This can lead to accidentally publishing  your app with debug information.", "more_info_urls": ["https://goo.gle/HardcodedDebugMode"], "category": "SECURITY", "severity": "FATAL", "priority": 5, "quality_tier": "MEDIUM", "test_methods": 2, "positive_cases": 1, "negative_cases": 2, "issue_covered_in_test": true, "difficulty": "EASY", "weighted_score": 2, "api_surfaces": ["manifest", "XML attribute scanning"], "scanner_interfaces": ["XmlScanner"], "loc": 80, "in_benchmark": true, "benchmark_split": "easy"}
